    {
      "id": "md2025_2282",
      "subset": "S5",
      "task_type": "cross-company-year-hybrid",
      "question": "In their Item 7 MD&A, which company explicitly states that they provide quantitative information about the impact of changes in volume and pricing on sales, and at which organizational level do they report this? Provide textual evidence from both ECL's FY2022 and LIN's FY2024 filings, and identify which financial table or note is referenced for additional segment detail.",
      "expected_answer": "ECL's FY2022 Item 7 states: 'We provide quantitative information about the material sales drivers including the impact of changes in volume and pricing and the effect of acquisitions and changes in foreign currency at the corporate and reportable segment level.' LIN's FY2024 Item 7 does not contain a similar explicit statement; instead it directs readers to 'Note 18 to the consolidated financial statements for additional information related to Linde’s reportable segments.' This Note 18 constitutes the financial table referenced for segment details.",
      "predicted_answer": "**Conclusion:** ECL (FY2022) explicitly states in its Item 7 MD&A that it provides quantitative information about the impact of changes in volume and pricing on sales, reporting this at **both the corporate and reportable segment level**. LIN (FY2024) does not contain an equivalent explicit statement about providing such quantitative information; instead, LIN presents volume and pricing factors in segment-level tables without a declaratory disclosure about the practice itself.\n\n**ECL FY2022 textual evidence:** \"We provide quantitative information about the material sales drivers including the impact of changes in volume and pricing and the effect of acquisitions and changes in foreign currency at the **corporate and reportable segment level**.\" [E1]\n\n**LIN FY2024 textual evidence:** LIN does not include a parallel explicit statement. The filing presents \"Factors Contributing to Changes - Sales\" tables showing Volume, Price/Mix, Cost pass-through, Currency, and Acquisitions/Divestitures percentages for each segment (Americas, EMEA, APAC, Engineering, Other) [E2][E3][E11], but does not declare that it \"provides quantitative information about the impact of changes in volume and pricing on sales.\"\n\n**Referenced table/note for additional segment detail:**\n- **ECL FY2022:** The MD&A segment performance tables (e.g., Global Institutional & Specialty, Global Healthcare & Life Sciences, Other) include Volume and Price changes as line items [E8][E10]; the filing also directs readers to **\"the tables within the section entitled 'Results of Operations' of this MD&A\"** for reconciliation information [E1].\n- **LIN FY2024:** The segment detail is presented in the **reportable segment table showing Sales, Variable Costs, Fixed Costs, Depreciation and Amortization, and Operating Profit by segment** [E12][E13][E14], with **Note 3 referenced for \"Cost reduction program and other charges\"** in the operating profit reconciliation [E5][E11].\n\n---\n\n**Sources**\n[E1] ECL_2022.html — Item 7. Management’s Discussion and Analysis of Financial Condition and Results of Operations.\n[E2] LIN_2024.html — Item 7. MANAGEMENT’S DISCUSSION AND ANALYSIS OF FINANCIAL CONDITION AND RESULTS OF OPERATIONS\n[E3] LIN_2024.html — Item 7. MANAGEMENT’S DISCUSSION AND ANALYSIS OF FINANCIAL CONDITION AND RESULTS OF OPERATIONS\n[E5] LIN_2024.html — Item 7. MANAGEMENT’S DISCUSSION AND ANALYSIS OF FINANCIAL CONDITION AND RESULTS OF OPERATIONS\n[E8] ECL_2022.html — Item 7. Management’s Discussion and Analysis of Financial Condition and Results of Operations.\n[E10] ECL_2022.html — Item 7. Management’s Discussion and Analysis of Financial Condition and Results of Operations.\n[E11] LIN_2024.html — Item 7. MANAGEMENT’S DISCUSSION AND ANALYSIS OF FINANCIAL CONDITION AND RESULTS OF OPERATIONS\n[E12] LIN_2024.html — Item 7. MANAGEMENT’S DISCUSSION AND ANALYSIS OF FINANCIAL CONDITION AND RESULTS OF OPERATIONS\n[E13] LIN_2024.html — Item 7. MANAGEMENT’S DISCUSSION AND ANALYSIS OF FINANCIAL CONDITION AND RESULTS OF OPERATIONS\n[E14] LIN_2024.html — Item 7. MANAGEMENT’S DISCUSSION AND ANALYSIS OF FINANCIAL CONDITION AND RESULTS OF OPERATIONS",
