      "task_type": "cross-company-year-hybrid",
      "question": "Compare the language used by LIN in FY2024 and ECL in FY2022 regarding the provision of quantitative sales driver information. Does LIN's FY2024 Item 7 mention quantitative sales drivers at all, or does it rely solely on references to financial tables? Support your answer with exact quotes from both filings and indicate which fiscal years are represented.",
      "expected_answer": "ECL's FY2022 Item 7 states: 'We provide quantitative information about the material sales drivers including the impact of changes in volume and pricing and the effect of acquisitions and changes in foreign currency at the corporate and reportable segment level.' LIN's FY2024 Item 7 does not contain any mention of quantitative sales drivers; it only states: 'Item 7, Management's Discussion and Analysis, for a discussion of consolidated sales and Note 18 to the consolidated financial statements for additional information related to Linde’s reportable segments.' Thus, LIN relies entirely on referencing the financial tables (Note 18) rather than providing quantitative descriptions in the text.",
      "predicted_answer": "**Conclusion:** LIN's FY2024 Item 7 explicitly discusses quantitative sales drivers in narrative text, not solely relying on table references. ECL's FY2022 Item 7, by contrast, emphasizes non-GAAP adjusted measures without providing comparable quantitative driver breakdowns in the retrieved evidence.\n\n- **LIN FY2024:** Narrative text quantifies drivers directly. Consolidated sales: \"Sales grew 2% from higher price attainment. Volumes were flat... Cost pass-through... decreased sales by 1%... Currency translation decreased sales by 1%\" [E2][E6]. Americas segment: \"Higher pricing contributed 3% to sales... net acquisitions increased sales by 1%... Cost pass-through decreased sales by 1%... Currency translation decreased sales by 2%... Volumes remained flat\" [E7][E8]. EMEA: \"Cost pass-through decreased sales by 4%... Higher price attainment increased sales by 3%. Volumes decreased sales by 1%\" [E5]. APAC: \"Volumes increased 2%... Currency translation decreased sales by 2%... Cost pass-through increased sales by 1%. Pricing was flat\" [E1][E5].\n\n- **ECL FY2022:** Retrieved evidence shows no quantitative sales driver narrative. Instead, ECL discusses non-GAAP measures: \"Fixed currency sales,\" \"Adjusted net sales,\" \"Acquisition adjusted fixed currency sales or organic sales\" [E3], and states these \"are useful for period-to-period comparison of results\" [E3]. No percentage-point breakdowns of volume, price, currency, or mix impacts appear in retrieved text or tables [E3][E4].\n\n**Comparison:** LIN FY2024 integrates explicit percentage contributions from volume, price/mix, currency, cost pass-through, and acquisitions directly into MD&A narrative, supplemented by tables. ECL FY2022's retrieved Item 7 evidence lacks any comparable quantitative driver decomposition, focusing instead on non-GAAP measure definitions.\n\n**Sources:**\n[E1] LIN_2024.html — Item 7. MANAGEMENT'S DISCUSSION AND ANALYSIS OF FINANCIAL CONDITION AND RESULTS OF OPERATIONS\n[E2] LIN_2024.html — Item 7. MANAGEMENT'S DISCUSSION AND ANALYSIS OF FINANCIAL CONDITION AND RESULTS OF OPERATIONS\n[E3] ECL_2022.html — Item 7. Management's Discussion and Analysis of Financial Condition and Results of Operations\n[E4] ECL_2022.html — Item 7. Management's Discussion and Analysis of Financial Condition and Results of Operations\n[E5] LIN_2024.html — Item 7. MANAGEMENT'S DISCUSSION AND ANALYSIS OF FINANCIAL CONDITION AND RESULTS OF OPERATIONS\n[E6] LIN_2024.html — Item 7. MANAGEMENT'S DISCUSSION AND ANALYSIS OF FINANCIAL CONDITION AND RESULTS OF OPERATIONS\n[E7] LIN_2024.html — Item 7. MANAGEMENT'S DISCUSSION AND ANALYSIS OF FINANCIAL CONDITION AND RESULTS OF OPERATIONS\n[E8] LIN_2024.html — Item 7. MANAGEMENT'S DISCUSSION AND ANALYSIS OF FINANCIAL CONDITION AND RESULTS OF OPERATIONS",
